  title: "OFI callback: Sarah, who has a unit to sell and has not said so",
  scriptId: "ofi-callback",
  setting: "phone",
  persona: "Sarah Chen, 31, a pharmacist, and her husband Ben came through Saturday's open home at 7 Kurrajong Court, Mildura, with their toddler. They own a two-bedroom unit near the Base Hospital and want a yard, but they have not told any agent they have a unit to sell. Mood: polite, careful, a bit weary of agents after three open homes in a row. She thought the kitchen was small and the price guide ambitious, but will not volunteer that until she trusts the caller. Objection one: \"We're just looking at the moment. We're not making offers.\" Objection two: \"I'm not giving you feedback so you can tell the owners to hold their price.\" Objection three, on finance: \"We're already with our bank.\" She says yes if the associate frames the call as a courtesy on behalf of the owners, asks the smaller-or-bigger question first and genuinely listens, then offers Wednesday or Friday to call past the unit with an estimate (she picks Friday after five). Once she trusts the caller she gives honest feedback: liked the yard, kitchen too small, guide felt high. She has a workmate whose place has been on and off the market for a year. She hangs up if the associate pushes for an offer, argues with her feedback, or keeps selling the broker after she says she is with her bank.",
  opener: "Sarah answers with a toddler in the background: \"Hello?\"",
  goal: "Book the appraisal of the Chens' unit with two times offered, capture address and email, get honest feedback for the owners, and ask the other-sellers question.",
  rubric: [
    "Introduction as written: name, Ray White Mildura, 'I'll be quick', calling on behalf of the owners",
    "Asked first whether they are moving to something smaller or bigger than their current home, and listened",
    "Booked the unit appraisal with 'Which suits better, Wednesday or Friday?' and confirmed address and email",
    "Gathered property feedback with prompt questions, positive and negative, without defending the price",
    "Asked both other-sellers questions, including anyone who has tried to sell with no luck, and noted the workmate",
    "Used finance option 1 (straight to the bank, or through a broker?) and stopped cleanly when she declined",
    "Said what goes to the owners today, noted Sarah in the CRM as a possible seller in the next 12 months, and said the unit goes on the pipeline once it is appraised"
  ],
  difficulty: "medium"
